<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<topic id="9473b45f-5001-4440-a0ca-c4adddb69235" revisionNumber="1">
  <developerConceptualDocument
    xmlns="http://ddue.schemas.microsoft.com/authoring/2003/5"
    xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">

    <introduction>
      <para>The <codeEntityReference qualifyHint="false">T:DemiCode.Scheduling.Tasks.CodeTask</codeEntityReference>
                executes a method on a .NET class. This is usefull in scenarios where you have existing .NET classes that performs
               some job and you need to configure your scheduler to execute this jobs on schedule.</para>
    </introduction>

    
                                    

<section>
  <content>
    <code language="xml">
            &lt;CodeTask class=&quot;Importer, MyLibrary&quot; method=&quot;ImportOrders&quot; /&gt;
            </code>
  </content>
</section>
    
        

<section>
  <title>Attributes and Elements</title>
  <content>
    
	<table>
		<title>Attributes</title>
                
		<tableHeader>
			<row>
				<entry>Attribute</entry>
				<entry>Description</entry>
			</row>
		</tableHeader>
			<row>
				<entry><legacyBold>class</legacyBold></entry>
				<entry>
					Fully qualified type name of a class that the CodeTask should instanciate. The class must have a public default constructor.
				</entry>
			</row>
			<row>
				<entry><legacyBold>method</legacyBold></entry>
				<entry>
					Name of a method on the class. If any <legacyBold>parameter</legacyBold> attributes exist, the method signature must have the same number
                                    of parameters.
				</entry>
			</row>
			<row>
				<entry><legacyBold>parameter</legacyBold></entry>
				<entry>
					Optional attribute(s).<para/>The parameter attribute can have any valid attribute name other than &quot;class&quot; and &quot;method&quot; and represents
                                    parameters passed to the <legacyBold>method</legacyBold> when executed. One or more attributes can be declared as long as the names are unique.
				</entry>
			</row>
	</table>
                
   <table>             
		<title>Child Elements</title>
                
		<tableHeader>
			<row>
				<entry>Element</entry>
				<entry>Description</entry>
			</row>
		</tableHeader>
			<row>
				<entry>
					<legacyBold><link xlink:href="100acdd4-daa3-4e8d-b09d-ad27d242a4af">scheduleref</link></legacyBold>
				</entry>
				<entry>
					Reference to a schedule that this task should be associated with.
				</entry>
			</row>
	</table>
	
    <table>             
		<title>Parent Elements</title>
                
		<tableHeader>            
			<row>
				<entry>Element</entry>
				<entry>Description</entry>
			</row>
		</tableHeader>
			<row>
				<entry>
					<legacyBold><link xlink:href="6204c862-a7b7-45a5-b870-08b3771a7308">tasks</link></legacyBold>
				</entry>
				<entry>
					Collection of one or more <legacyBold>task</legacyBold> elements.
				</entry>
			</row>
	</table>
  </content>
</section>
         
            
    

